{"file":"CrowdSec Skill-0.3.0-v2.zip","bytes":154298,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"crowdsec","description":"CrowdSec skills: an operational skill (install/configure/operate/debug the engine, cscli, bouncers, WAF and bot detection across bare-metal/Docker/Kubernetes) and a Service API skill (drive the premium Console cloud API — blocklists, allowlists, firewall integrations, metrics, decisions).","version":"0.3.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec-skill","homepage":"https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec-skill","keywords":["crowdsec","security","waf","appsec","bouncer","fail2ban","console","service-api","sapi","blocklist","integration","cloud","bot-detection","bot-management","challenge"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/crowdsec-service-api/SKILL.md","name":"crowdsec-service-api","description":"Use when the user wants to drive the CrowdSec Console **Service API (SAPI)** — the premium cloud REST API at admin.api.crowdsec.net — to programmatically manage blocklists (add/remove/bulk IPs, share, subscribe engines), allowlists, firewall/appliance integrations (Palo Alto, Fortinet, Cisco, F5, Sophos, pfSense/OPNsense…), remediation ROI metrics, and org-level decisions. Acts on the user's behalf with their API key. This is the cloud/API skill — for the local engine, cscli, and bouncers use the `crowdsec` skill.","headings":["CrowdSec Service API (SAPI) — cloud blocklist / allowlist / integration automation","Boundary — this skill vs the `crowdsec` skill","Operating contract","→ {\"organization_id\":\"…\",\"subscription_type\":\"…\",\"api_key_name\":\"…\"}","Step — Detect the intent","Step — curl cheat sheet","Hard don'ts","Docs"],"name_hint":"crowdsec · service · api","description_zh":"使用用户API密钥调用CrowdSec Console付费云Service API，管理阻断与允许名单、批量IP、名单共享、引擎订阅、防火墙集成、处置ROI及组织决策；本地引擎操作交给crowdsec技能。"},{"path":"skills/crowdsec/SKILL.md","name":"crowdsec","description":"Use when the user is installing, configur